/// The terminal stage of the git push pipeline: it matches a normalized push
/// event's remote URLs against the remote-to-slug map it is configured with and
/// pulls the matched repositories through the `git-repo-pull` tool, one async
/// call per push. The call's result arrives later on `tool-results`, the
/// component's inbox for the tool substrate, where each repository's outcome is
/// logged, alerted on when it failed, and republished on `outcomes`.
///
/// Every capability is load-bearing and none is optional: `config` carries the
/// remote-to-slug map, without which no push matches anything; `store` holds
/// the monotonic counter the async call ids come from, so a pull cannot be
/// issued without it; `alert` is how a failed pull reaches an operator, which
/// is the whole point of running the pipeline unattended; `tools` is the
/// authority to call `git-repo-pull` at all.
///
/// The map is written in the instance's `config = { ... };` attr, whose surface
/// is flat: `repo_slugs` is a comma-separated index of the slugs this instance
/// syncs, and one `remote_<slug>` entry per listed slug holds that repository's
/// remote URL. A listed slug with no `remote_<slug>` entry, an empty remote
/// value, or a slug listed twice fails the activation.
component GitSyncConsumer {
  abi = processor;
  requires = [ports, log, store, alert, config, tools];
  in push-events;
  in tool-results;
  out outcomes;
}
